---
// Privacy.
//
// THE ONE TRUST PAGE THAT CAN BE WRITTEN IN FULL TODAY, because it describes
// what the code does rather than a fact only Ric holds. Every sentence below is
// checkable against this repo, and that is the standard it is written to — a
// privacy policy assembled from a template is the same lie as an invented
// delivery cost, just longer and less likely to be read.
//
// CLAUDE.md requires this page and a working marketing opt-out with the first
// deploy. The honest form of the opt-out here is that there is no marketing list
// and nothing subscribes anyone to one: the only use of an email address is the
// receipt the buyer asked for. That is a statement to keep true rather than a
// box to tick — if a mailing list is ever added, this page changes first.
//
// Deliberately NOT dated. A "last updated" line is a fact like any other and it
// is the first thing to rot; the file's history in the repo is the real record.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — MomentAura"
  description="What this site collects, what it does not, and how long anything is kept."
  system="light"
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap page__inner">
      <h1 class="page__heading">Privacy</h1>

      <p class="page__body">
        This page describes what the site actually does. Everything here can be checked
        against how the site behaves.
      </p>

      <hr class="page__hair" />

      <h2 class="page__sub">What is not collected</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        There are no analytics on this site. No tracking pixels, no advertising tags, no
        session recording, no third-party scripts of any kind. The fonts are served from
        this site rather than from a font network, so loading a page does not tell anyone
        else that you did.
      </p>
      <p class="page__body">
        There are no accounts and no passwords, so there is no store of credentials to
        lose. There are no cookies. Checking an order needs its reference and the phone
        number it was placed with, and nothing more.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">What your browser stores</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        Your order is kept in your own browser's local storage while you shop, and it
        holds only the product code and how many of each — never a name, a price or a
        stock figure. It never leaves your device until you go to checkout. Clearing your
        browser data removes it, and nothing here can read it back.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">What is collected when you order</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        Your name, your phone number, and an email address if you choose to give one. The
        email is optional and is only ever used to send you a receipt. Nothing subscribes
        you to anything, because there is no mailing list to subscribe to.
      </p>
      <p class="page__body">
        Your phone number is required because M-Pesa sends the payment prompt to it. Your
        name and phone number are passed to the payment provider to take the payment, and
        to nobody else.
      </p>
      <p class="page__body">
        <strong>No card details are ever entered on this site.</strong> Payment happens on
        the payment provider's own secure page. This site has no card form anywhere in it
        and never will.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">How long it is kept</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        A pending order — the product codes, the quantities, the amount, your name, your
        phone number and the email if you gave one — is held for seven days so the payment
        can be matched to the order and so you can look it up. After that it expires
        automatically.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">Who else sees it</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        The payment provider, because they are taking the payment. The company hosting
        this site, because the pages and the order have to pass through it. Nobody else.
        Nothing is sold, shared for advertising, or handed to a data broker.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">Asking for it to be removed</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        Ask on the <a href="/contact">contact</a> page with your order reference and the
        record will be deleted, except where a payment record has to be kept to account
        for money that actually moved.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    background-color: var(--bg);
    color: var(--fg);
    padding-block: var(--s-56) var(--s-80);
  }

  .page__inner {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
  }

  .page__heading {
    font-size: var(--t-heading);
    margin-block-end: var(--s-40);
  }

  .page__sub {
    font-size: var(--t-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-label);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin-block-end: var(--s-16);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-40);
  }

  .page__body {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-block-end: var(--s-20);
  }

  .page__hair {
    border: 0;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--border);
    width: 100%;
    margin-block: var(--s-40);
  }
</style>
